  "question": {
    "text": "The hydrogen electrode is dipped in a solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The potential of the electrode will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Round off the answer to the nearest integer.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,<br/>pH =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi>log</mi><mo> </mo><mo>[</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>[</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>The half cell reaction is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></msub></math></p><p>We know,</p><p>the Nernst equation is<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>red</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo> </mo><mi>log</mi><mo> </mo><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi>log</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo> </mo><mo>×</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>177</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p>",
